{"summary":"dxi-mcp-server: Detect AppData connector credential fields from toolkit schema.json for out-of-band secure capture","description":{"type":"doc","version":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Project: "},{"type":"inlineCard","attrs":{"url":"https://github.com/delphix/dxi-mcp-server.git","localId":"e73a805e8767"}},{"type":"text","text":" , main branch"}],"attrs":{"localId":"3b70a9528c39"}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"localId":"6bd40157b99b"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Today, when a workflow needs a credential and the user is on a generic MCP client (Claude Desktop/Code, VS Code Copilot), the secret is typed straight into the prompt, so it ends up in the LLM context. The DCT AI Assistant avoids this. It has a separate secure-input UI that captures the credential and injects it into the request out-of-band, so the LLM never sees it. That mechanism is already built: the "},{"type":"text","text":"sensitive_input_required","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" gate in "},{"type":"text","text":"src/dct_mcp_server/tools/core/dynamic.py","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Step 3.5), scoped to capture-capable hosts (DLPXECO-14641/14642/14650)."}],"attrs":{"localId":"2fb9f34183fb"}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"localId":"c382a6d8b599"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Problem"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gate decides which fields are credentials "},{"type":"text","text":"only","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from the "},{"type":"text","text":"x-dct-toolkit-credential-field","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" annotation in the DCT OpenAPI spec ("},{"type":"text","text":"_CREDENTIAL_FIELD_ANNOTATION","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" / "},{"type":"text","text":"_annotated_credential_fields()","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"attrs":{"localId":"3666c400914f"}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This works for native Delphix data sources. It does not work for "},{"type":"text","text":"AppData (toolkit/connector-based) sources","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" such as DB2, MySQL, SAP HANA, MongoDB and Couchbase. For those, the DCT spec models connector parameters as a free-form object (e.g. "},{"type":"text","text":"appdata_source_params","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" / linked-source and virtual-source parameters), so it says nothing about which attributes a connector accepts or whether any of them are secrets."}],"attrs":{"localId":"8c3739b8f465"}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The only source of truth is the connector's own "},{"type":"text","text":"schema.json","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", which ships with the toolkit. In that schema a credential is declared with "},{"type":"text","text":"\"format\": \"password\"","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Virtualization SDK convention)."}],"attrs":{"localId":"7cf0988e7e35"}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As a result, AppData credentials (e.g. DB2 instance password, MySQL DB user password) never trigger the secure-input UI in the DCT AI Assistant. They get passed inline through the LLM context."}],"attrs":{"localId":"dd83e513becb"}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"localId":"3c0f6da0aa07"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed Change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to the OpenAPI annotation, derive credential fields from the connector schema:"}],"attrs":{"localId":"9589c621a133"}},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"order":1,"localId":"afb66ca3309f"},"content":[{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"7c78eceff28d"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Resolve the toolkit","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for the operation being executed (e.g. from "},{"type":"text","text":"toolkit_id","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the body, or from the source/environment/dSource referenced by the request) for AppData operations: link/create dSource, provision VDB, update dSource/VDB params, add/update source configs, etc."}],"attrs":{"localId":"3cc919a5359b"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"bd24b8684bd8"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fetch the toolkit's schema definitions","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from DCT (toolkit details expose the plugin's "},{"type":"text","text":"linkedSourceDefinition","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"virtualSourceDefinition","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"repositoryDefinition","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"sourceConfigDefinition","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshotParametersDefinition","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"attrs":{"localId":"f671c1cd4b8b"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"b11def0587d9"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Walk the JSON schema recursively","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":", including nested objects, arrays, "},{"type":"text","text":"items","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"oneOf","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"/"},{"type":"text","text":"anyOf","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"/"},{"type":"text","text":"allOf","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"text","text":"$ref","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"s. Collect every property with "},{"type":"text","text":"\"format\": \"password\"","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and record its path relative to the parameters object."}],"attrs":{"localId":"a64b191c4f24"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"074351319a43"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Merge","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" these fields with "},{"type":"text","text":"_annotated_credential_fields(spec)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when evaluating "},{"type":"text","text":"_missing_sensitive_fields()","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for that request. Match them scoped to the AppData parameters sub-object, not globally by name, so a generic name like "},{"type":"text","text":"password","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in a connector schema cannot flag unrelated fields."}],"attrs":{"localId":"9f54550e97ec"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"8d3d292e132c"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Raise ","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":"sensitive_input_required","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for those fields exactly as for spec-annotated ones. The DCT AI Assistant then shows its secure credential UI for them, and "},{"type":"text","text":"sensitive_applied","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" handling, host-nonce validation and host scoping stay unchanged."}],"attrs":{"localId":"6f06b4ff95f5"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"099e8dbab925"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cache","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the derived credential set per toolkit (id + version) so the schema isn't re-fetched on every call."}],"attrs":{"localId":"36058d696fe9"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"c96141ced9c6"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Expose it in discovery.","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" When describing an AppData operation's parameters, mark connector password-format fields as secrets so the model knows not to ask for them in chat."}],"attrs":{"localId":"d028e4a663c8"}}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"localId":"20827c7fd3ad"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Acceptance Criteria"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"0aa8a4a078e0"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] For an AppData operation (e.g. DB2 or MySQL dSource link / VDB provision) on a capture-capable host, every connector parameter declared "},{"type":"text","text":"\"format\": \"password\"","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the toolkit "},{"type":"text","text":"schema.json","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" triggers "},{"type":"text","text":"sensitive_input_required","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when missing or supplied inline. This includes nested properties."}],"attrs":{"localId":"0fea824b1f50"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"93cd88f8d735"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] The DCT AI Assistant shows the secure credential UI for those fields, and the value reaches DCT without entering the LLM context."}],"attrs":{"localId":"1d1958812c71"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"faa319190818"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] Re-calls with the field supplied via "},{"type":"text","text":"sensitive_applied","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (valid nonce) succeed and do not re-prompt (no regression of DLPXECO-14603)."}],"attrs":{"localId":"c5889c21e977"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"9b2b7e715fd4"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] Non-password connector fields (usernames, ports, paths, ids) are never flagged."}],"attrs":{"localId":"6efae813862b"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"891edb5acbb9"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] Native (non-AppData) operations behave exactly as today, still driven by "},{"type":"text","text":"x-dct-toolkit-credential-field","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"attrs":{"localId":"acda896ac06e"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"f91015f8cb54"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] Non-capture-capable clients (Claude Desktop/Code, VS Code Copilot) behave as today. The gate stays host-scoped (DLPXECO-14642)."}],"attrs":{"localId":"021b23858100"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"2ccf2292cd8d"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] If the toolkit schema can't be fetched or parsed, the server logs a warning and falls back to spec-annotation-only behaviour. The operation is not blocked."}],"attrs":{"localId":"64a52264bc6b"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"3b76b798505d"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[ ] Unit tests cover the schema walker (nested, arrays, combinators, "},{"type":"text","text":"$ref","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), path-scoped matching, caching and fallback. Integration tests cover at least DB2 and MySQL toolkits."}],"attrs":{"localId":"10a34f83031b"}}]}],"attrs":{"localId":"515cbf611563"}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"localId":"45dd948cf052"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"c4750246399a"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Relevant code: "},{"type":"text","text":"tools/core/dynamic.py","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"text","text":"_annotated_credential_fields","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"_collect_missing_secrets","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"_missing_sensitive_fields","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", Step 3.5 gate. Tests: "},{"type":"text","text":"tests/test_sensitive_input_gate.py","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"tests/integration/test_sensitive_gate_scoping.py","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"attrs":{"localId":"d33973601dcd"}}]},{"type":"listItem","attrs":{"localId":"fb538e653b31"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Related: DLPXECO-14641, DLPXECO-14642, DLPXECO-14650, DLPXECO-14603."}],"attrs":{"localId":"3dbc6972aea7"}}]}],"attrs":{"localId":"50d15420c850"}}]},"issuetype":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10015","id":"10015","description":"Created by Jira Agile - do not edit or delete. Issue type for a user story.","iconUrl":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium","name":"Story","subtask":false,"avatarId":10315,"hierarchyLevel":0},"labels":["AI-IN-PROGRESS"],"components":[],"reporter":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6167ab769cdb93007204c6f2","accountId":"6167ab769cdb93007204c6f2","emailAddress":"shreyas.kulkarni@perforce.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png"},"displayName":"Shreyas Kulkarni","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Chicago","accountType":"atlassian"},"assignee":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6167ab769cdb93007204c6f2","accountId":"6167ab769cdb93007204c6f2","emailAddress":"shreyas.kulkarni@perforce.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/310dc3ec1e1b3cd7ddc7566084da2cdc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSK-3.png"},"displayName":"Shreyas Kulkarni","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Chicago","accountType":"atlassian"}}
